ost infinity saga  of the mcu and this is what brad  winterbomb  executive producer had to say in  response well  yeah i mean it's no coincidence that  this show picks up  right after loki you know the spoiler at  the end of loki and i am about to talk  about the finale so spoiler warning she  says the multiverse has now  erupted in every possible direction and  what if gives us a chance to explore  that and i think you can tell  that in this next saga the multiverse is  gonna be  crucial then if you combine that with  what the writer ac bradley had to say in  an interview with ign  we pretty much get full confirmation  that what if is  canon to the mcu to the mcu's multiverse  she confirmed this in the interview by  saying the multiverse is here  it's real and it's absolutely fantastic  people  what if is just a part of the multiverse  and some of these stories could bleed  into the main  sacred timeline our timeline that loki  introduced and i personally asked ac  bradley if seeing captain carter show up  down the road in the mcu  say in multiverse of madness is a  possibility and this is what her  and director brian andrews had to say i  would give anything to write peggy  carter again hopefully we'll get to see  her more in the show but  that's up to powers greater than me  well i think you absolutely showed that  because  like i said just get started off with  her it's a great start her kicking butt  it's pretty cool to watch on screen and  i really wish we could have  seen that or we can see that live action  uh you know this morning during the  press conference uh brad  winterbomb mentioned that there's  potential for characters to show up down  the road in  the mcu perhaps maybe in like multiverse  of madness or something where there's  rumors flying around right now any any  chance we do see her later on  in the mcu maybe uh  that is stuff that's going on probably  above and beyond us  we all would love that you know as soon  as that's the k i mean we're just like  anyone else  who doesn't even work at marvel it's  like there's there's stuff that we don't  know  uh right because kevin's the lord  overseer and he's got like stuff going  on that  we might be unaware of but it would be  amazing uh  i think both ac and i would love to see  some  you know haley atwell in that suit live  action kicking ass  being amazing we'd all love that yeah so  even though of course they can't tell us  yes this person is going to be in this  live-action  marvel project they do seem very hopeful  they both said that they hope it happens  and they'd love to see it happen  and apparently i'm not the only person  asking this question because in the  press conference somebody else  asked i just watched loki and were  waiting for spider-man and doctor  strange movies and it's not just comic  fans now but every mcu fan knows about  the multiverse can we expect some of  these events of  what if to be a part of the mcu movies  as well  in which executive producer brad  winterbomb responded by saying  yeah i mean i think that without going  into great detail i can tell you that  what if as a project as a story that  exists  in the mcu as you know as important as  any other it's woven into that same  tapestry  these fun little threads there's gonna  be a lot of potential there  and specifically in regards to captain  carter it does really seem like she's  very important  to marvel or at least the writers of  what if and i asked ac bradley  why captain carter is such a driving  force to what if and could be such a  driving force to the mcu in the future  i love peggy carter i've loved her since  her first moment  in the first avenger from agent carter  to and beyond  i think the reason i fell so hard for  peggy carter and then writing captain  carter  was in the show we explored the  different sides of all the heroes we  explored the different sides of thor we  explore a different side of tony but  they're already heroes they're already  super powered up they already have all  the toys  peggy what does she have she's a woman  who knows her worth  and then i got to give her some super  powers i got to say  hells yeah let's show let's make the uh  the outside final match the inside let's  see who she is  yeah and that was such an honor and to  top this all off during the press  conference i actually got to personally  ask a question  to jeffrey wright jeffrey of course is  playing the watcher in marvel's what if  and here was my question to him  the watcher was such an amazing  character and he's so important in  marvel in general  is the watcher appearing in the mcu in a  live action  movie or show something that we could  possibly see or something he would want  to do  and this is his response well what if  is very much about the idea that all  things are  possible so you know and then he took a  second and laughed for a little bit and  said  that's a reasonable question and i guess  the answer to it  is well what if now he didn't really  give me a confirmation of course  he can't but he did put a very good  question out there and it's ironic but  it is  what if what if is a part of the  multiverse that is the mcu right now and  if one character can come from one  universe to another there's no reason  that the watcher from this animated  universe can't come into our main mcu  timeline and be the watcher of that  and like he did say anything is possible  now from here i'd just like to talk  about  the show what if my thoughts on it and  answering some questions that i've had a  lot of you ask me that i actually got  answered during the press conference  one question is are these shows going to  connect to each other or are they going  to be  one off and i've seen the first three  episodes and they were all completely  different they did not connect at all  at least not that we know of so far but  brad wonderbomb actually answered this  question  he said it's an anthology there are  standalone  stories and they're really much like the  films they exist on their owns and  they're trying to create stories  that exist on their own terms so if you  were to watch any episode of what if and  that's the only episode you watched you  get a  full experience hopefully with the  character  that lives a rich life and changes  dynamically and is entertaining and  emotionally satisfying  but at the same time during the press  conference a question was asked if we  are going to see  characters like captain carter or  t'challa as star-lord pop  up in other stories beyond their  introductory episodes in the first  season  and what brad wunderbaum had to say was  early on in the development they started  to realize that some  characters had more story arcs than the  others not necessarily  more important but had a strong  relationship with  the watcher who is a big driving force  behind the series  and we realized as we started developing  a second season that captain carter was  gonna be the character we would revisit  so captain carter is going to return in  season  two and hopefully she'll return in a  multiverse of madness as well but we'll  have to wait and see on that  now for the film fans out there and the  actor fans and people who like to know  about the process  i did ask director brian andrews what it  was like to have  all of these famous mcu actors do  voice-overs and this is what he had to  say  yeah no they're very casual you know  they don't have to worry about it except  for sometimes if they're at their  in their in their in their in their  closet yeah they're very casual but  sometimes we get them to come into  like a particular studio or vietnam or  whatever there's some  you know once things start to open up a  little bit people can get back into a  a venue and record out in there so they  had to look you know  a little bit more normal but they  wouldn't have hours of makeup to be a  hero you know what i mean it's  it's still like sure i'm gonna roll in  and do some 